{"book":18,"chapter":26,"context":{"chapter":26,"title":"The Fringes of His Ways","summary":"Job mocks Bildad's 'help,' then describes God's power over the world of the dead, the skies, the clouds and the sea, concluding that all this is only 'parts of his ways.'","background":"The poem uses ancient cosmic images: God hangs the earth 'upon nothing' (v. 7), binds water in clouds, draws a boundary at the edge of light and darkness, and strikes down Rahab (KJV 'the proud') and 'the crooked serpent.' 'Destruction' in verse 6 is Abaddon, a name for the realm of the dead (Revelation 9:11). Some scholars assign verses 5–14 to Bildad.","customs":[],"watchFor":["The closing line: 'how little a portion is heard of him? but the thunder of his power who can understand?' (v. 14).","Job's sarcasm (vv. 2–4) before the hymn."],"connections":["Isaiah 27:1","Proverbs 15:11","Isaiah 51:9","Revelation 9:11"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיַּעַן","vaiya'an","H6030","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he answered"],["אִיּוֹב","'iyov","H347","HNpm","Job"],["וַיֹּאמַר","vaiyomar","H559","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he said"]]},"2":{"w":[["מֶה","meh-","H4100","HPi","how!"],["עָזַרְתָּ","'azarta","H5826","HVqp2ms","you have helped"],["לְלֹא","lelo'-","H3808","HR/Tn","<to> not"],["כֹחַ","khoach","H3581","HNcmsa","power"],["הוֹשַׁעְתָּ","hosha'ta","H3467","HVhp2ms","you have saved"],["זְרוֹעַ","zeroa'","H2220","HNcfsa","[the] arm"],["לֹא","lo'-","H3808","HTn","not"],["עֹז","'oz","H5797","HNcmsa","strength"]],"x":[[18004003,18004004,3],[23035003,23035004,3]],"xn":2},"3":{"w":[["מַה","mah-","H4100","HPi","how!"],["יָּעַצְתָּ","ya'atzta","H3289","HVqp2ms","you have counseled"],["לְלֹא","lelo'","H3808","HR/Tn","<to> not"],["חָכְמָה","chokhmah","H2451","HNcfsa","wisdom"],["וְתוּשִׁיָּה","vetushiyah","H8454","HC/Ncfsa","and sound wisdom"],["לָרֹב","laro","H7230","HR/Ncmsa","for abundance"],["הוֹדָעְתָּ","hoda'eta","H3045","HVhp2ms","you have made known"]]},"4":{"w":[["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["מִי","mi","H4310","HPi","whom?